From c323c2d8d27dfd6809e015c0c6b505edddc1291b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c-drew <101952850+c-drew@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:20:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Render thread: cheaper chunk rebuild queue and block
 entity pass

- Rebuild queue: a ConcurrentLinkedQueue plus a queued-index set instead of a
  ConcurrentHashMap iterated and cleared every frame. Iterating or clearing a CHM walks its
  whole table, which stays at its peak size after a burst of rebuilds (world load, travel).
  Chunks enqueued while draining are no longer dropped by the trailing clear().
- Block entities: chunks rebuilt with block entities are indexed instead of walking every
  chunk section each frame, and the index is re-verified 1/60 of the storage per frame (a
  full re-scan every 60th frame spiked: render distance 32, 1% low 91 -> 109 fps with the
  spread re-check). Block entities the dispatcher would not draw (no
  renderer, unsupported state, out of range) are skipped before buffers are allocated.
- Per-object vertex storage starts at 16 KB instead of 768 KB and render layer names are
  encoded to native strings once (upstream issue #252).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014aGN7pt3GAnXQRSSREgQzx
